    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0306" n="194" xml:id="pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4019</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>)</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Britannic Majesty’s
                    Ambassador and in reply to the Embassy’s Memorandum No. 171 of March 5, 1919,
                    has the honor to state that Minister Reinsch was informed of the reference of
                    the matter in question to the British Minister at Peking and was instructed to
                    consult with the latter concerning the request received by the British
                    Government from the Union of Chinese Workmen in Russia and to telegraph his
                    views.</p>
                <p>Minister Reinsch has replied that it is felt that Bolshevik propaganda would find
                    little material in China to work on as no social or class distinctions exist. He
                    states that the Chinese Government is willing to have the workmen in question
                    return but wants to know when and where they will enter China, for it is felt
                    that among them are Manchurian bandits who might cause local trouble unless
                    supervised.</p>
                <p>Advices received by the Department of State from other sources indicate that the
                    request from the Union of Chinese Workmen now under consideration is part of a
                    plan for promoting an armed uprising of Bolsheviks in Siberia and for carrying
                    on revolutionary propaganda and establishing Soviets in China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-03-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1919</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
